<article class="env-lemma" id="0B2M">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B2M">Lemma <span data-tag="0B2M">33.20.5</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$, $Y$ be locally algebraic $k$-schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
For $z \in X \times Y$ lying over $(x, y)$ we have $\dim _ z(X \times Y) = \dim _ x(X) + \dim _ y(Y)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We have $\dim (X \times Y) = \dim (X) + \dim (Y)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Proof of (1). Consider the factorization 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X \times Y \longrightarrow Y \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       of the structure morphism. The first morphism $p : X \times Y \to Y$ is flat as a base change of the flat morphism $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01U9" data-tag="01U9">29.26.8</a>. Moreover, we have $\dim _ z(p^{-1}(y)) = \dim _ x(X)$ by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FY" data-tag="02FY">29.29.3</a>. Hence $\dim _ z(X \times Y) = \dim _ x(X) + \dim _ y(Y)$ by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02JS" data-tag="02JS">29.29.2</a>. Part (2) is a direct consequence of (1). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>